########## 2. Invalid requests are rejected by the API server (nothing is created)
--- unknown size (XL)

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: bad }
spec: { teamName: bad, size: XL, repoURL: "http://git.example/bad.git" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "bad" is invalid: 
* spec.size: Unsupported value: "XL": supported values: "S", "M", "L"
* <nil>: Invalid value: null: some validation rules were not checked because the object was invalid; correct the existing errors to complete validation
-> rejected, as expected
--- missing teamName

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: nameless }
spec: { size: S, repoURL: "http://git.example/x.git" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "nameless" is invalid: 
* spec.teamName: Required value
* <nil>: Invalid value: null: some validation rules were not checked because the object was invalid; correct the existing errors to complete validation
-> rejected, as expected
--- missing size

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: nosize }
spec: { teamName: nosize, repoURL: "http://git.example/x.git" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "nosize" is invalid: 
* spec.size: Required value
* <nil>: Invalid value: null: some validation rules were not checked because the object was invalid; correct the existing errors to complete validation
-> rejected, as expected
--- invalid team name (uppercase, underscore)

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: bad }
spec: { teamName: Bad_Name, size: S, repoURL: "http://git.example/x.git" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "bad" is invalid: 
* spec.teamName: Invalid value: "Bad_Name": spec.teamName in body should match '^[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$'
* <nil>: Invalid value: "object": metadata.name must equal spec.teamName (one environment per team)
-> rejected, as expected
--- repoURL is not a URL

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: badurl }
spec: { teamName: badurl, size: S, repoURL: "not-a-url" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "badurl" is invalid: spec.repoURL: Invalid value: "not-a-url": spec.repoURL in body should match '^https?://[^\s/]+(/[^\s]*)?$'
-> rejected, as expected
--- metadata.name differs from teamName

$ [cp1] kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
apiVersion: platform.kiratech.io/v1alpha1
kind: TeamEnvironment
metadata: { name: one }
spec: { teamName: other, size: S, repoURL: "http://git.example/x.git" }
EOF
The TeamEnvironment "one" is invalid: <nil>: Invalid value: "object": metadata.name must equal spec.teamName (one environment per team)
-> rejected, as expected

$ [cp1] kubectl get teamenvironments
No resources found

